      </div>
      <div class="cmp" data-rv style="--d:140ms">
        <div class="cmp__hd">
          <span>Who</span>
          <span class="trk"><span>Find</span><span>Screen</span><span>Interview</span><span>Write the verdict</span></span>
          <span>Then it's yours</span>
        </div>
        {
          compareRows.map(([name, stopLabel, stagesReached, desc, isUs]) => (
            <div class:list={['cmp__r', isUs && 'cmp__r--us']}>
              <p class="cmp__n">{name}</p>
              <span class="cmp__stop">{stopLabel}</span>
              <span class="trk">
                {[0, 1, 2, 3].map((i) => (
                  <span class:list={['seg', i < stagesReached && 'on', i === stagesReached - 1 && 'last']} />
                ))}
              </span>
              <p class="cmp__l">{desc}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <p class="cmp__ft">
        Segments are sized by where the hours actually go — finding people is quick, forming a defensible
        view is not. <b>Everybody stops one stage short of the same thing.</b>
      </p>

      <p class="says" data-rv>
        "Before tribera I used to walk in explaining my shortlist. Now I walk in with a decision. They
        trust it because I trust it."
        <span>Head of Talent Acquisition · global GCC, 3,000+ employees</span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ VOICES: both sides of it ═══ -->
  <section class="band band--w" id="voices">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--red" data-rv>Both sides of it</p>
          <h2 class="h2" data-rv style="--d:60ms">What they say afterwards.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="dek" data-rv style="--d:100ms">
          The hiring teams who stopped explaining their shortlists, and the people who stopped applying.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <!-- Doubled so the CSS marquee (.mq__t) can scroll seamlessly from the first
         copy straight into the second. -->
    <div class="mq" data-rv style="--d:140ms">
      <div class="mq__t">
        {
          [...testimonials, ...testimonials].map(([kind, quote, name, role]) => (
            <figure class:list={['qc', `qc--${kind}`]}>
              <span class="qc__tag">{kind === 'ta' ? 'Hiring team' : 'Candidate'}</span>
              <blockquote class="qc__q">{quote}</blockquote>
              <figcaption class="qc__a">
                <b>{name}</b>
                <span>{role}</span>
              </figcaption>
            </figure>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ THE DEAL: interview three, hire one ═══ -->
  <section class="deal band" id="guarantee">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--red" data-rv>The deal</p>
          <h2 class="h2" data-rv style="--d:60ms">Interview three. Hire one.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="deal__dek" data-rv style="--d:100ms">
          The industry average is eight interviews per hire. We commit to three — and we can, because
          <b>your team still interviews every person we send</b>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="pledge2" data-rv style="--d:130ms">
        All three must be hireable. <em>If none of them fit, we restart at no cost.</em>
      </p>
      <p class="pledge2__s" data-rv style="--d:150ms">
        Written into every engagement agreement — not a clause buried in the contract, and not a
        ninety-day window either.
      </p>

      <!-- Volume tiers (10-50 / 50-200 / 200-500+) are picked from and rendered by the
           deal-volume script below; the markup here is just the tab strip and the
           containers it fills in (#volNm, #volV, #volD, #volPts). -->
      <div class="vol" data-rv style="--d:170ms">
        <p class="vol__k">How many hires a year?</p>
        <div class="vol__ax" role="tablist" aria-label="Engagement volume">
         <button class="vseg" role="tab" data-i="0" aria-selected="false"><span></span><i>10 - 50</i></button>
         <button class="vseg is" role="tab" data-i="1" aria-selected="true"><span></span><i>50 - 200</i></button>
         <button class="vseg" role="tab" data-i="2" aria-selected="false"><span></span><i>200 - 500+</i></button>
        </div>

        <div class="vol__out" id="volOut">
          <div class="vol__l">
            <p class="vol__nm" id="volNm">Scale</p>
            <p class="vol__v" id="volV">50 - 200 <span>hires a year</span></p>
            <p class="vol__d" id="volD">
              Several functions running at once, with one bar carried across all of them.
            </p>
            <a href="#close" class="btn btn--light">Brief a role</a>
          </div>
          <ul class="vol__pts" id="volPts" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="incl" data-rv>
        <p class="incl__k">In every engagement, whichever shape</p>
        <div class="incl__g">
          <span>Three expert-validated people per brief</span>
          <span>You interview all three. Always.</span>
          <span>No setup fee, no retainer</span>
          <span>Brief changes? We redo it free</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ ENGAGE: from brief to hire, and who does what ═══ -->
  <section class="band band--w" id="engage">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--red" data-rv>How we engage</p>
          <h2 class="h2" data-rv style="--d:60ms">From brief to hire — and who does what.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="dek" data-rv style="--d:100ms">
          Forty-five minutes to learn your yes. Thirty-six hours to the shortlist.
          <b>Then your team runs the interviews, with the rubric already in their hands.</b>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="cg__g" data-rv style="--d:140ms">
        {
          engageSteps.map(([date, dateSuffix, title, desc, who]) => (
            <div class="cg">
              <span class="cg__bar" />
              <p class="cg__d">
                {date} <i>· {dateSuffix}</i>
              </p>
              <p class="cg__t">{title}</p>
              <p class="cg__p">{desc}</p>
              <p class="cg__w">{who}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <div class="estat" data-rv>
        {
          engageStats.map(([number, unit, desc]) => (
            <div class="estat__i">
              <p class="estat__n">
                {number}
                <i>{unit}</i>
              </p>
              <p class="estat__d">{desc}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <div class="cg__notes" data-rv>
        {
          engageNotes.map(([title, body]) => (
            <div>
              <p class="cg__k">{title}</p>
              <p class="cg__v">{body}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ TRUST: the AI recommends, a person decides ═══ -->
  <section class="trust band" id="trust">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow" data-rv>Trust and compliance</p>
          <h2 class="h2" data-rv style="--d:60ms">The AI recommends. A person decides. Always.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="trust__dek" data-rv style="--d:100ms">
          Built for a world of candidate data, consent and fair evaluation —
          <b>the questions your legal team and DPO ask before the first brief.</b>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tr2" data-rv style="--d:140ms">
        {
          compliance.map(([title, items]) => (
            <div class="tr2__c">
              <p class="tr2__k">{title}</p>
              <ul class="tr2__l">
                {items.map((item) => <li set:html={item} />)}
              </ul>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <div class="path" data-rv>
        <p class="path__k">Where a decision can actually be made</p>
        <div class="path__g">
          {
            decisionPath.map(([num, title, desc, tag, isYou]) => (
              <div class:list={['path__s', isYou && 'path__s--you']}>
                <span class="path__n">{num}</span>
                <p class="path__t">{title}</p>
                <p class="path__d" set:html={desc} />
                <span class:list={['path__tag', isYou && 'path__tag--you']}>{tag}</span>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="qa" data-rv>
        <p class="qa__q">"Can an algorithm reject my candidates?"</p>
        <p class="qa__a">No. It surfaces and explains. <em>The reject is always human.</em></p>
      </div>

      <p class="trust__ft" data-rv>
        ISO 27001 and SOC 2 certification underway, with core controls operating today. Role-based,
        least-privilege access, audit-logged. Every brief documented in the system, so the context sits
        with the engine rather than with one person.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ HINGE: the 1:3 ratio, from both sides ═══ -->
  <section class="wrap band--t">
    <div class="hinge">
      <div data-rv>
        <p class="hg__k">If you're hiring</p>
        <p class="hg__t">Interview three. Hire one.</p>
        <p class="hg__d">
          Your best people stop spending Thursdays on candidates who were never getting past round two.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="hg__mid" data-rv style="--d:80ms">
        <p class="hg__n">1:3</p>
        <div class="ratio">
          <div class="ratio__r">
            <span class="ratio__k">Industry</span>
            <span class="ratio__sq"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i class="hit"></i></span>
          </div>
          <div class="ratio__r ratio__r--us">
            <span class="ratio__k">tribera</span>
            <span class="ratio__sq"><i></i><i></i><i class="hit"></i></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="ratio__ft">Interviews per hire</p>
        <div class="cost" id="cost">
          <div class="cost__r">
            <span class="cost__k">Usual</span>
            <span class="cost__b"><span class="cost__f" style="--w:100%" /></span>
            <span class="cost__v">32 <i>hrs</i></span>
          </div>
          <div class="cost__r cost__r--us">
            <span class="cost__k">tribera</span>
            <span class="cost__b"><span class="cost__f" style="--w:37.5%" /></span>
            <span class="cost__v">12 <i>hrs</i></span>
          </div>
          <p class="cost__ft">
            Panel time per hire, at four people an interview.
            <b>Twenty hours back, every seat you fill.</b>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div data-rv style="--d:160ms">
        <p class="hg__k">If you're looking</p>
        <p class="hg__t">If a team asks for you, they mean it.</p>
        <p class="hg__d">
          You're not one of eight in a pile. You're one of three, and they've read your interview before
          the call.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ CANDIDATES: interviewed once, shortlisted everywhere ═══ -->
