          <p class="fan__was">One conversation with us</p>
          <span class="fan__3"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span>
          <p class="fan__cap">
            <b>Three teams asked for him inside 48 hours.</b> Not applications — requests, from teams who
            had read his interview before they picked up the phone.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="qt" data-rv>
        "The expert had already read my GitHub. The first question was about a design decision I made in
        2022. That's when I knew this was different."
        <span>Senior backend engineer, six years' experience</span>
      </p>

      <p class="human" data-rv>
        We built this because we'd all been on your side of the table, <em>and we remembered how it felt</em>.
      </p>
      <p class="human__b" data-rv>
        And if you're the one hiring — <b>this is why the people we send you pick up the phone.</b> Nobody
        arrives at your interview having been treated badly on the way in.
      </p>

      <div class="expect" data-rv>
        <div class="expect__hd">
          <p class="expect__k">What you can expect from us, every time</p>
          <a class="expect__lk" href="/candidates">The whole thing, in detail →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="expect__g">
          {
            candidateExpectations.map(([title, desc]) => (
              <div>
                <b>{title}</b>
                <span>{desc}</span>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="apply" id="apply" data-rv>
        <p class="apply__k">Start here</p>
        <h3 class="apply__h">Drop your CV. We'll take it from there.</h3>
        <p class="apply__s">
          Leave your email and we'll pick it up on the next screen — your name and CV, about a minute.
          <b>We reply within a day either way</b>, and if we can't help we'll say so rather than go quiet.
        </p>
        <form class="apply__form" action="/candidates" method="get">
          <div class="apply__row apply__row--2">
            <input
              class="apply__mail"
              type="email"
              name="email"
              required
              placeholder="your@email.com"
              aria-label="Your email address"
            />
            <button class="apply__go" type="submit">Continue<span class="apply__ar">→</span></button>
          </div>
        </form>
        <p class="apply__fine">
          No account needed · <b>one minute, two fields</b> · your email is only ever used to reply ·
          <a href="/candidates" style="color:var(--onc);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px">
            see how it works first
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
